message.content:
Use the CSS **`:hover`** pseudo-class on the `span` and set its `color` there. The `:hover` selector matches an element when the cursor is over it, and it works on all elements, not just links.[5][6]

```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.hover-text {
  color: black;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If you want the color to change smoothly, add a transition:

```css
.hover-text {
  color: black;
  transition: color 0.2s ease;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the `span` contains other elements or the color is not changing, check for more specific CSS rules overriding it; inline styles and more specific selectors can take precedence.[1][5]

